          bullets: [
            "Vetspire: Built-in clinical decision support originally designed for teaching hospitals — surfaces relevant protocols during patient care",
            "This category is still early-stage — expect significant expansion over the next 2 years as LLMs integrate into clinical tools",
            "Diagnostic AI (analyzing lab results, imaging) is still primarily handled by specialist tools outside PIMS",
          ],
        },
        {
          heading: "Which Practices Benefit Most from AI Features?",
          body: "AI features are not equally valuable for every practice. Here is where the ROI is strongest:",
          bullets: [
            "High-volume general practices: More appointments = more documentation time saved",
            "Solo veterinarians: Every hour saved on notes is directly recovered for patient care or personal time",
            "Practices with documentation backlogs: If notes are routinely completed after hours, AI can reclaim that time",
            "Growing practices: AI scales with volume without adding administrative staff",
            "Practices with high associate turnover: AI reduces onboarding time for new veterinarians who join without deep note-taking habits",
          ],
        },
        {
          heading: "Questions to Ask AI-Powered PIMS Vendors",
          body: "When a vendor claims AI features, ask these specific questions to separate genuine ML from marketing:",
          bullets: [
            "Is the AI trained on veterinary clinical data specifically, or is it a general language model?",
            "How does the SOAP note generation work — does it require a template prompt, or does it learn from the appointment itself?",
            "Can I see a live demo on a real case, not a pre-scripted example?",
            "What is the accuracy rate on your clinical note generation? How is that measured?",
            "What data is used to train the AI, and where is my practice data stored?",
          ],
        },
      ],
      faqs: [
        {
          question: "Does AI veterinary software actually work?",
          answer: "For SOAP note generation specifically: yes, it works, and the time savings are real. Digitail's Tails AI and Onward Vet's speech-to-text have genuine user reviews documenting meaningful documentation time reduction. The quality varies by case complexity — straightforward wellness visits benefit most, while complex multi-system cases may still require significant manual editing.",
        },
        {
          question: "Is AI in veterinary software safe for patient care?",
          answer: "Current AI features in veterinary PIMS assist with documentation, not with clinical decisions. The veterinarian still makes all diagnostic and treatment decisions — the AI just reduces the time spent writing them up. Clinical decision support features (like those in Vetspire) surface guidelines but do not replace veterinary judgment. Always review AI-generated notes before finalizing.",
        },
        {
          question: "How much extra does AI veterinary software cost?",
          answer: "In most cases, AI features are bundled into the standard subscription rather than sold as a separate add-on. Digitail includes Tails AI in its base plan starting at $299/mo per veterinarian (Standard plan). Onward Vet starts at $300/mo per practice with AI included. Compared to the time saved, the cost premium over non-AI PIMS is minimal.",
        },
        {
          question: "What is the best AI veterinary software?",
          answer: "For automated SOAP notes: Digitail (Tails AI) is the most established and widely reviewed AI PIMS in the market. Onward Vet is the most innovative but newer and less proven at scale. Both offer free trials — we recommend testing each with real clinical cases before deciding.",
        },
      ],
      relatedTools: ["digitail", "onward-vet", "vetspire"],
      relatedLinks: [
        { href: "/best/best-veterinary-software-with-ai", label: "Best AI Veterinary Software" },
        { href: "/reviews/digitail", label: "Digitail Review" },
        { href: "/reviews/onward-vet", label: "Onward Vet Review" },
        { href: "/guides/how-to-choose-veterinary-software", label: "How to Choose Vet Software" },
      ],
    },
  };

  return Object.keys(guides).map((slug) => ({
    params: { slug },
    props: { guide: guides[slug] },
  }));
}

interface Props {
  guide: GuideContent;
}

const { slug } = Astro.params;
const { guide } = Astro.props;

// Resolve related tools
const relatedTools = guide.relatedTools
  .map((s) => getToolBySlug(s))
  .filter(Boolean) as any[];

// Build FAQ schema
const faqSchemaJson = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: guide.faqs.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.answer },
  })),
});

const articleSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: guide.title,
  description: guide.description,
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "VetSoftwareHub" },
  datePublished: "2026-02-25",
  dateModified: "2026-02-25",
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title={guide.title}
  description={guide.description}
  canonical={`https://vetsoftwarehub.com/guides/${slug}`}
  ogTitle={guide.ogTitle}
  ogDescription={guide.ogDescription}
  schema={{ "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: guide.ogTitle }}
>
  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs">
    <a href="/" class="text-navy-400 hover:text-accent-600 transition-colors">Home</a>
    <span class="text-navy-300">/</span>
    <a href="/guides" class="text-navy-400 hover:text-accent-600 transition-colors">Guides</a>
    <span class="text-navy-300">/</span>
    <span class="text-navy-600">{guide.ogTitle}</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Header -->
  <header class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 sm:text-4xl leading-tight">
      {guide.ogTitle}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-navy-600">{guide.intro}</p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-xs text-navy-400">
      <span>By VetSoftwareHub Editorial Team</span>
      <span>Last updated: February 2026</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Table of Contents -->
  <nav class="mb-10 rounded-xl border border-navy-100 bg-navy-50/30 p-5" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <h2 class="font-heading text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-navy-500">In This Guide</h2>
    <ol class="mt-3 space-y-1.5">
      {guide.sections.map((section, i) => (
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="shrink-0 text-xs font-bold text-accent-500">{i + 1}.</span>
          <a href={`#section-${i}`} class="text-sm text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 transition-colors">
            {section.heading}
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
        <span class="shrink-0 text-xs font-bold text-accent-500">{guide.sections.length + 1}.</span>
        <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 transition-colors">FAQ</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <!-- Sections -->
  <div class="space-y-12 mb-14">
    {guide.sections.map((section, i) => (
      <section id={`section-${i}`}>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900 sm:text-3xl">
          {i + 1}. {section.heading}
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-navy-600">{section.body}</p>
        {section.bullets && (
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
            {section.bullets.map((bullet) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-navy-700">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-accent-500" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.704 4.153a.75.75 0 01.143 1.052l-8 10.5a.75.75 0 01-1.127.075l-4.5-4.5a.75.75 0 011.06-1.06l3.894 3.893 7.48-9.817a.75.75 0 011.05-.143z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
                </svg>
                <span>{bullet}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <!-- Related Tools -->
  {relatedTools.length > 0 && (
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">Tools Referenced in This Guide</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {relatedTools.map((tool: any) => (
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy-100 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-navy-900">{tool.name}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-navy-500">{tool.tagline}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-semibold text-navy-800">
              {tool.starting_price_monthly !== null ? `From $${tool.starting_price_monthly}/mo` : "Custom pricing"}
            </p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex gap-2">
              <a
                href={`/reviews/${tool.slug}`}
                class="text-xs font-medium text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 transition-colors"
              >
                Read review →
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <!-- Email Capture -->
  <div class="mb-14">
    <EmailCapture
      heading="Get Our Free Vet Software Buyer's Guide"
      subheading="The complete guide to choosing, pricing, and switching veterinary PIMS. Join 1,000+ practice managers."
    />
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" class="mb-14">
    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">
      {guide.sections.length + 1}. Frequently Asked Questions
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-3">
      {guide.faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group rounded-lg border border-navy-100 bg-white">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 font-heading font-semibold text-navy-800 transition-colors hover:text-accent-600">
            {faq.question}
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.168l3.71-3.938a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="border-t border-navy-100 px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            {faq.answer}
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Related Links -->
  <nav class="rounded-xl border border-navy-100 bg-white p-6" aria-label="Related content">
    <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-navy-900">Related Resources</h3>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {guide.relatedLinks.map((link) => (
        <li>
          <a href={link.href} class="text-sm text-accent-600 underline decoration-accent-200 underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-700 hover:decoration-accent-400 transition-colors">
            {link.label}
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- Schema -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchemaJson} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={articleSchema} />
</BaseLayout>
